# MUI

When editing StoreDesk Electron UI that uses Material UI:

1. Read `.cursor/skills/react-dev/SKILL.md` for typed React/TS patterns when building/editing components.
2. Read `.cursor/skills/mui/SKILL.md` for sx/theme/component patterns.
3. For deep styling or component examples, open the matching file under `.cursor/skills/mui/resources/`.
4. Apply `.cursor/skills/storedesk-ui/SKILL.md` for StoreDesk page structure (PageShell, no subtitles, flat outlined surfaces).
5. For official API docs, use MUI MCP: `useMuiDocs` then `fetchDocs`.
6. Use theme tokens (`primary.main`, `text.secondary`, spacing scale) — no hardcoded hex in pages.
7. Prefer `Stack` / `Box` + shared `components/ui` primitives over one-off layout.
8. Prefer navy/green brand tones only — no glow KPIs or rainbow accent kits.
9. Large UI redesigns: `review-gate` via eng-manager + `ui-ux-designer` before ship.
